            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I hit this again on a recent nightly (a few days old: e715122e4e).\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-813+ge715122e4e\nBuild type: RelWithDebInfo\nLuaJIT 2.1.1774896198\n\nIt was a never-ending spam of this message:\n\n<img width=\"2008\" height=\"343\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cbdfc4e4-bbcc-4890-864d-231d887e52a2\" />\n\nUnfortunately, the message no longer includes the failing file.\n\nI was working on the same project as above, so same lua-ls and harper-ls active lsp.\n\nThis time, I was editing `.git/info/exclude`, did a `git pull --rebase` outside of nvim, when I focused nvim (running in neovide) it gave this error. The error spam is so nonstop that I can't give ex commands and nvim won't even respond to the window's X close button.\n\nCould `watch()` gracefully handle the error instead of asserting? It looks like it later tracks some kinds of errors and returns an empty function which I assume prevents further file access? If EPERM is a reasonable error, then maybe we should abort the watcher?",
